   "finding": "Day pass under thin cold cloud (S8 ~255-260 K). The two strongest mid-infrared anomalies in the whole frame lie on the fire: S7 peak 304.4 K (+17 K over local median) in the 1 km pixel at the origin (52.776, -110.92), and F1 peak 303.6 K (+18 K) in the pixel about 1.5 km east-southeast, covering Range 2 and the road head (52.771, -110.90). The S7 and F1 peaks are offset by about one pixel, consistent with known registration differences between SLSTR's fire and thermal channels and with daytime sunlight in the mid-infrared; location finer than 'the fire area' is not supported. Acquisition time not in the export."
